# Which results the REPL echoes: a `none` is shown only when the statement
# AS TYPED is a value lookup (a name, none / null, a member or subscript
# step last, the whole of it parenthesized) and hidden for a call, an
# operator, a declaration. An input that fails while it runs keeps the
# bindings its completed statements made and gives back the rest; one
# refused before it runs gives back everything it declared, in both
# scopes. :globals names what each clone is for.
